      "text": "Understanding the difference between needs and wants is crucial for making sound financial decisions and maintaining a healthy budget."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "What Are Needs?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Needs are essential items and services required for basic survival and functioning in society:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Housing and utilities",
        "Basic food and water",
        "Healthcare",
        "Basic transportation",
        "Essential clothing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "What Are Wants?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Wants are items and services that enhance life but aren't essential for survival:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Entertainment subscriptions",
        "Luxury clothing and accessories",
        "Dining out",
        "Latest gadgets",
        "Vacations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "How to Prioritize"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Follow these steps to make better financial decisions:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        "List all your regular expenses",
        "Categorize them as needs or wants",
        "Ensure needs are covered first",
        "Budget for wants from remaining funds",
        "Save before spending on wants"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The 50/30/20 Rule"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A popular budgeting method:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "50% for needs",
        "30% for wants",
        "20% for savings and debt repayment"
      ]
    }
